  "id": "COMPOUND:22402 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, multi-step relationship between the compound (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and Phosphodiesterase 6C. The compound is identified as a target of multiple agents, including 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, 1-Hydroxycyclocolorenone, and Khrinone C, all of which are known to interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates that the compound may act as a modulator or inhibitor of Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that the compound may influence the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C via a pathway involving sialyltransferase activity, as the compound directly targets this enzyme. The presence of multiple targets and the consistent interaction with Phosphodiesterase 6C across different pathways supports the hypothesis that the compound may exert its effect through a mechanism that involves the regulation of sialyltransferase activity, which in turn affects Phosphodiesterase 6C. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between the compound and Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
